# sudo rule for the Xymon "powerline" server collector.
#
# Debian/Ubuntu installs this as /etc/sudoers.d/my-xymon-extensions-server
# (root:root 0440, a conffile) with the rule COMMENTED OUT, because
# powerline ships disabled. To grant it, remove the "#" from the last line
# and run visudo -c. Elsewhere, install it yourself:
#   visudo -c -f powerline.sudoers
#   install -o root -g root -m 0440 powerline.sudoers \
#       /etc/sudoers.d/my-xymon-extensions-server
# Keep the file name free of dots: sudo ignores such files in sudoers.d.
#
# powerline-read.sh allows only fixed read-only plcstat/plcrate queries
# with validated arguments. The rule is only as safe as the helper's path:
# if xymon can write the helper or any parent directory, it is a root
# shell (postinst checks this). Never grant powerline.sh, a shell or the
# plc tools themselves.

#xymon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: @BINDIR@/powerline-read.sh
